# THE TEST MAP (SPEC.md 137.54.6, 2026-11-20): the BZDEV=1 build's pathway in place of path.bbc - the rows'
# map, never shipped (`test`: bbcourse.py -o refuses it without --dev).  Its pads play the TEST courses
# (137.54) besides the two shipped ones, so bonanzapath's legs walk a map built for them and depend neither on
# the shipped map's shape (which is redrawn as real courses ship) nor on a prototype course.  Each route is
# one feature the rows need:
#
#   page 1 (above):        5 TMIL (1 unit up)
#                          ^ up-right, UP A RAMP (the CLIMB; TPLY's exit 0)
#                          4 TPLY [icon]
#                          ^ up, across the page line (the PAGED camera; TCUP's exit 0)
#   page 0 (below):  3 TCUP <-up-left (the DIAGONAL: Up and Left; TQUIK's exit 0)- 2 TQUIK -right..> 6 BENCH
#                                                                         ^ up      (SECRET: TQUIK's hidden exit 1,
#                                                                         |          a SIDE pad, hidden)
#                                                    0 ROLL -right-> 1 HOP   (STRAIGHT: the shipped map's pads 0
#                                                                             and 1, cell for cell)
#
# Pads 0 and 1 and their route are the shipped map's exactly (cells, icons, ROLL's exit 0 the key), so what a
# row does on the shipped map's first two pads it does here unchanged (Enter on pad 0 plays ROLL, pad 1's way
# back is Left alone).  A screen direction is a ground step: +x down-right, -x up-left, +y down-left, -y
# up-right; both axes at once (equal amounts) down, up, left or right.
course PATH "The Test Map"
test                                        # SPEC.md 137.54.6: a TEST MAP - the BZDEV=1 build's alone, its pads
                                            # may play test courses
width  64
ball   rubber
pathway
music  fairway
rail   crystal
view   0 332                                # page 0's CGA window, the shipped map's
pages  2
titles 5x7
float  rect 0 0 64 64

# pad N COURSE WX WY
pad 0 ROLL  21 28                           # the shipped map's pad 0: where a new game rests
pad 1 HOP   24 25                           # the shipped map's pad 1
pad 2 TQUIK 19 20                           # the goal course; its hidden exit 1 the secret route's key
pad 3 TCUP  14 20                           # the diagonal's far end
pad 4 TPLY   9 15                           # page 1, the ICON pad
pad 5 TMIL   9 11                           # page 1, 1 unit up: the climb's end (a dead end)
pad 6 BENCH 23 16                           # HIDDEN: only the secret route reaches it (a SIDE pad)

# route A B exit E [secret] [gate WX WY] path WX,WY[,H] ...
route 0 1 exit 0  path 21,28 24,25                  # STRAIGHT across (Right; Left back): the shipped map's
route 1 2 exit 0  path 24,25 19,20                  # straight UP
route 2 3 exit 0  path 19,20 14,20                  # the DIAGONAL, up-left along -x: Up and Left both take it
route 3 4 exit 0  path 14,20 9,15                    # straight up ACROSS THE PAGES (page 0 -> page 1)
route 4 5 exit 0  path 9,15 9,13,1 9,11,1           # up-right UP A RAMP (one cell, 1 unit): the CLIMB
route 2 6 exit 1 secret  path 19,20 23,16           # the SECRET route, TQUIK's hidden exit 1: right to a hidden pad

# icon N FILE SX SY [fps F] [title "TEXT"] [tdx DX]
icon 0 icons/first32x24.bba       -128 368          # (the shipped map's)
icon 1 icons/frog32x24.bba         -32 368          # (the shipped map's)
icon 4 icons/playground32x24.bba  -112 168          # the ICON leg's pad (the far end of the page route)

# the lives, one counter a page
lives 16 23
lives  6  4
